# Playwright Conventions

## Tagging

Every `test` carries **exactly one** Playwright suite tag — never on `test.describe`. Pick the slice that best describes **why** the test runs, not the ticket id (use the title or file name for traceability).

| Tag | Use when |
|-----|----------|
| `@smoke` | Minimal critical path after deploy or auth setup |
| `@sanity` | Short post-change check of one feature area |
| `@regression` | Broader functional coverage, edge UI, accessibility specs, mocked network cases |
| `@api` | Asserts primarily through HTTP/API (setup, contract, or direct API behavior) |
| `@e2e` | Full UI journey through the app with real backend (default for most Didaxis flows) |
| `@destructive` | Mutates **shared or global** state only — org locale, roles, feature flags, tenant settings, or other data other tests depend on |

**Not `@destructive`:** creates that `trackProgram` (or similar) deletes in the same run, or other data scoped to that test. Keep `@smoke`, `@sanity`, `@regression`, `@api`, or `@e2e` instead.

**`@destructive` runs:** wrap in `test.describe.configure({ mode: 'serial' })`. CI and local slices use `npm run test:destructive` (`--workers=1`). Any test that mutates shared/global state — including `@destructive` — must **revert in `test.afterEach` or `test.afterAll`** (restore prior locale, role, flag, or setting). Do not leave the environment dirty for parallel suites.

```typescript
test.describe('Org locale', () => {
  test.describe.configure({ mode: 'serial' });

  let savedLocale: string;

  test.beforeEach(async ({ adminApi }) => {
    savedLocale = await adminApi.getOrgLocale();
  });

  test.afterEach(async ({ adminApi }) => {
    await adminApi.setOrgLocale(savedLocale);
  });

  test('admin can set org locale to fr-CA', { tag: '@destructive' }, async ({ page }) => {
    // ...
  });
});
```

```typescript
test('creates a program via the UI', { tag: '@e2e' }, async ({ programs, trackProgram }) => {
  const { name, description } = buildProgramHappyPath();
  trackProgram(await programs.createProgram(name, description));
});
```

Run slices: `npm run test:smoke`, `test:sanity`, `test:regression`, `test:api`, `test:e2e`, `test:destructive`.

## Auth

Stored session by default (`tests/auth.setup.ts` → `playwright/.auth/user.json`). UI login only when the test is the login page. API login (POST credentials, then inject the token) is for bulk setup, a one-off script, or a stale storageState.

```typescript
// Login-page test only
test.use({ storageState: { cookies: [], origins: [] } });
await new LoginPage(page).goto();
```

A feature spec does not call `/login` or write a password into source.

## Page Objects

One class per page or component in `pages/` (`LoginPage`, `ProgramsPage`, `NewProgramModal`). Locators are `readonly` in the constructor. Methods only go, click, fill, or submit. A page composes the components it contains. The spec states intent; every `expect` stays in `tests/`.

```typescript
const programs = new ProgramsPage(page);
await programs.openNewProgramForm();
await expect(programs.newProgramNameField).toBeVisible();
```

## Locators

`getByRole`, then `getByLabel` or `getByPlaceholder`, then `getByText`, then `getByTestId` with a comment on why nothing higher worked. Narrow a multi-match with `.filter({ hasText })`.

```typescript
this.dialog = page.getByRole('dialog', { name: 'New Program' });
this.programNameField = this.dialog.getByLabel('Program Name');
this.createButton = this.dialog.getByRole('button', { name: 'Create' });
```

No CSS selectors, XPath, brittle copy, or `.first()` on several matches.

## Test data

| Kind | Location | Notes |
|------|----------|--------|
| Happy-path generated values | `test-data/factories/` | `@faker-js/faker`; unique per run; override fields in the factory call |
| Invalid / boundary inputs | `test-data/invalid/*.ts` | Curated static sets — not random |
| Secrets and base URLs | `process.env` (e.g. `DIDAXIS_URL`, `DIDAXIS_API_TOKEN`) | Never in source |
| Repeated UI copy, routes, API paths | Enums or `const` objects (e.g. next to POMs or under `test-data/`) | Same string in two places → one export |

Example factory:

```typescript
// test-data/factories/program.factory.ts
import { faker } from '@faker-js/faker';

export function buildProgramHappyPath(overrides: Partial<{ name: string; description: string }> = {}) {
  const year = faker.number.int({ min: 2024, max: 2030 });
  return {
    name: `${faker.commerce.productAdjective()} ${faker.word.noun()} ${year} ${faker.string.alphanumeric(8)}`,
    description: faker.lorem.paragraph({ min: 1, max: 3 }),
    ...overrides,
  };
}
```

```typescript
import { buildProgramHappyPath } from '../test-data/factories/program.factory';
import { BLANK_PROGRAM_NAME } from '../test-data/invalid/program-names.invalid';

const { name, description } = buildProgramHappyPath();
const invalidName = BLANK_PROGRAM_NAME;
```

## Data and cleanup

Prefer `buildProgramHappyPath()` or factories in `test-data/factories/` for names and descriptions; use `uniqueSuffix()` from `tests/helpers/didaxis-programs.ts` when a legacy suffix helper is already in the spec. Import `test` from `fixtures/cleanup.fixture.ts` and call `trackProgram` with `data.id` from the real create response. The fixture deletes `DELETE /api/programs/<uuid>?purge=true` with `DIDAXIS_API_TOKEN`.

```typescript
import { expect, test } from '../fixtures/cleanup.fixture';
import { buildProgramHappyPath } from '../test-data/factories/program.factory';

const { name: programName, description } = buildProgramHappyPath();
trackProgram(await programs.submitCreateProgram(programName, description));
```

No manual `afterAll` cleanup for **self-owned** data (the fixture handles it). **Shared/global** mutators use `afterEach`/`afterAll` revert hooks (see Tagging). No hardcoded Bearer token, and no `trackProgram` on an id the test did not create.

## Waiting

Wait with a web-first assertion that retries: `expect(locator).toBeVisible()`, `.toBeEnabled()`, or `.toHaveText()`.

```typescript
await expect(programs.newProgramNameField).toBeVisible();
await expect(programs.newProgramCreateButton).toBeEnabled();
```

No `waitForTimeout`, and no one-shot `expect(await locator.isVisible()).toBe(true)`. A fixed sleep ends before the programs list refetches, and a boolean sampled once does not retry.

## Network mocking

Fulfill with `page.route` in the spec only the programs call that produces the UI state under test. Tag the test `{ tag: '@regression' }`. Assert copy already on the page object. Read the live page before writing the sentence. When the app renders nothing, assert `programs.heading` is visible and that no `pageerror` fired.

```typescript
test('empty list shows the empty state', { tag: '@regression' }, async ({ page }) => {
  await page.route('**/api/programs', async (route) => {
    const path = new URL(route.request().url()).pathname.replace(/\/$/, '');
    if (route.request().method() !== 'GET' || !path.endsWith('/programs')) {
      await route.continue();
      return;
    }
    await route.fulfill({
      status: 200,
      contentType: 'application/json',
      body: JSON.stringify({ data: [] }),
    });
  });
  const programs = new ProgramsPage(page);
  await programs.goto();
  await expect(programs.emptyProgramsText).toBeVisible();
});
```

The same shape covers `503` on `PATCH /programs/<id>`, a `200` body that is not a program array, and `404` / `400` / `403` / `500` / `501` on save, plus `401` / `502` / `504` / `300` on list load.

Do not mock the endpoint the test claims to verify, fulfill `**/api/programs/**` for every method, `trackProgram` a mocked id, or assert a sentence the live page does not render (`Service Unavailable`).

## Accessibility

Scan in `tests/<feature>.a11y.spec.ts` through `expectNoAxeViolations` with axe tags `wcag2a` and `wcag2aa`. Suite tag: `{ tag: '@regression' }` (one per test). Run the keyboard path through the POM inside `runCiSoftA11y`. A real violation is an info report (rule id, impact, target, help URL) and must not fail CI.

```typescript
test('has no WCAG 2 A or AA violations', { tag: '@regression' }, async ({ page }) => {
  const programs = new ProgramsPage(page);
  await programs.goto();
  await expect(programs.heading).toBeVisible();
  await expectNoAxeViolations(page, { tags: ['wcag2a', 'wcag2aa'] });
});

test('Enter on New Program opens the dialog', { tag: '@regression' }, async ({ page }) => {
  await runCiSoftA11y('programs-new-program-keyboard', async () => {
    const programs = new ProgramsPage(page);
    await programs.goto();
    await expect(programs.newProgramButton).toBeFocused();
    await page.keyboard.press('Enter');
    await expect(programs.newProgramDialog).toBeVisible();
  });
});
```

No bare `expect(results.violations).toEqual([])` in the spec, no `.disableRules()`, and no `.include()` / `.exclude()` without a comment naming the noisy third-party widget.

## Anti-flake

Keep `fullyParallel: true`, `retries: process.env.CI ? 2 : 0` (never above 2), `trace: 'on-first-retry'`, `baseURL` from `DIDAXIS_URL`, `locale` `en-US`, and `timezoneId` `America/Toronto`. Serialize only the describe that shares one admin. Freeze a relative timestamp with `page.clock.install` before navigation. Page objects do not install the clock.

```typescript
test.describe('DS-1: Create new academic program', () => {
  test.describe.configure({ mode: 'serial', timeout: 120_000 });

  test('creates a uniquely named program', { tag: '@e2e' }, async ({ programs, trackProgram }) => {
    const programName = `Data Analytics 2026 ${uniqueSuffix()}`;
    trackProgram(await programs.createProgram(programName, 'Full-stack web development program'));
    await expectProgramInList(programs, programName);
  });
});

test('row shows when the program was saved', { tag: '@regression' }, async ({ page }) => {
  await page.clock.install({ time: new Date('2026-10-30T16:00:00') });
  const programs = new ProgramsPage(page);
  await programs.goto();
  await expect(programs.programRow('Web Development')).toContainText('2 minutes ago');
});
```

Do not set `workers: 1`, `fullyParallel: false`, retries above 2, or another locale or timezone. Do not assert a relative label from `Date.now()` (`just now`, `2 minutes ago`, `today`).

## Refusals (hard stops)

Refuse these. Stop and raise the conflict.

- **Weaken or delete an assertion to pass.** Leave the assertion as written and report that the run is red because the check failed.
- **Heal a failure triage classified as a real bug.** Leave the spec and page object unchanged and report the defect for a human.
- **Replace a role-based locator with CSS or XPath.** Keep `getByRole` (then label, placeholder, text, or test id) and report that the selector change was refused.
- **Use `waitForTimeout`.** Report that a fixed sleep was refused. Wait with a web-first assertion that retries, such as `expect(locator).toBeVisible()`.
- **Hardcode a credential.** Report that a password, token, or Bearer secret in source was refused.
- **Use the `any` type.** Report that an untyped `any` was refused. Name the real type, or stop when the type is unknown.
